{"uid":"1e3de6aa0af75c64","name":"test_task_dialog_shows_more_than_the_current_status_task039","fullName":"tests.test_browser_hub#test_task_dialog_shows_more_than_the_current_status_task039","historyId":"13e9e94bd7ec48467ec3754e5f140550","time":{"start":1791938864022,"stop":1791938868523,"duration":4501},"description":"Task 039 (PRD I.1): a task detail dialog shows the STATES a task\n    passed through, with timestamps and (where recorded) a cause -- not\n    only its current status.\n\n    `engine.state.task_transition_history` reads this fact straight off\n    the run's own `events.jsonl` \"task\" events (`LoopSupervisor.\n    _emit_task_status`/`_emit_task_changes`, the only writers of that\n    event type) -- named here and in the commit message, per this task's\n    own success criteria.\n\n    Task `030` bounces pending -> in-progress -> pending (a worker\n    deferral, carrying `deferredReason`) -> in-progress -> completed, four\n    transitions recorded on `events.jsonl`, while `tasks.json` itself only\n    ever shows the LAST of those (`completed`) -- so the dialog listing\n    more than one state proves it is reading the transition log, not\n    re-deriving anything from the task's current status alone.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task 039 (PRD I.1): a task detail dialog shows the STATES a task<br />\npassed through, with timestamps and (where recorded) a cause -- not<br />\nonly its current status.</p>\n<pre><code>`engine.state.task_transition_history` reads this fact straight off\nthe run's own `events.jsonl` &quot;task&quot; events (`LoopSupervisor.\n_emit_task_status`/`_emit_task_changes`, the only writers of that\nevent type) -- named here and in the commit message, per this task's\nown success criteria.\n\nTask `030` bounces pending -&gt; in-progress -&gt; pending (a worker\ndeferral, carrying `deferredReason`) -&gt; in-progress -&gt; completed, four\ntransitions recorded on `events.jsonl`, while `tasks.json` itself only\never shows the LAST of those (`completed`) -- so the dialog listing\nmore than one state proves it is reading the transition log, not\nre-deriving anything from the task's current status alone.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791938101992,"stop":1791938101992,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791938101993,"stop":1791938101993,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_scrub_notifier_env_in_process","time":{"start":1791938864019,"stop":1791938864020,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791938864019,"stop":1791938864019,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791938864019,"stop":1791938864019,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_task_record_dir","time":{"start":1791938864019,"stop":1791938864019,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_stub_escalation_backoff_at_class_level","tim